summary:
The Frostbite scores in our paper were Josh Tenenbaum and @TomerUllman. My score, in fact, remains unpublished :)
Quoting @nicholdav
@jonothingEB @LakeBrenden mainly got into AI as a pretext to humblebrag about his FrostBite high scores

How does the mutual exclusivity bias change across development?
@mcxfrank @LakeBrenden @tammykwan, V. Cristiano, and I use meta-analytic data and developmental exps. to characterize the trajectory. We show that vocab knowledge is closely tied to change in bias strength.
📷 https://pbs.twimg.com/media/ESXyzULXkAAsP-I.jpg

CogSci 2020 will be virtual rather than in-person. Disappointed not to go to Toronto, but happy that we can still share our work.
@cogsci_soc is collecting ideas for a smooth virtual conference with multiple tracks, poster sessions, and participants in many time-zones.
📷 https://pbs.twimg.com/media/EUX6CTWVAAADg2Q.jpg

New from the lab:
A Bayesian approach to collinearity detection, which you could call a simple form of perceptual organization. We focus on the effects of uncertainty as controlled by retinal eccentricity.
@yanlisagezhou started this work as an.. 1/

Important point! Have been arguing we should use actual novel words for a while now in various talks and in my dissertation (Ch 5, actual argument Ch 5.2 3).
Quoting @LakeBrenden
@quocleix @ZoubinGhahrama1 Also, SCAN is about the idea that people can add a novel word like "dax" and seamlessly integrate it with other concepts. Using the English words makes these words not really "new" for the LLM. Curious if it would still work with nonsense words substituted in? (2/2)

it was meeeee
Quoting @OskuTorro
@rowancheung @gdb @sama @emilychangtv The timeline of "the last couple of weeks" matches with this discovery.

Thrilling (if long overdue) news of tenure for the brilliant and wonderful @ev_fedorenko! I am so very proud of you Ev (even though you were amazing when I first met you and I don't deserve any credit). I'm grateful beyond measure to have you as a colleague and friend.
Quoting @ev_fedorenko
@neuranna Thank you, friend @neuranna! And a big thank you to all those who have supported me across all the different stages of this long, and often difficult, journey (you know who you are &lt;3). I really wish my parents were here: I wouldn't be here without them and I miss them every day.

I'm looking forward to speaking at this AI + Society + Philosophy symposium later this week. I'm glad it's a symposium rather than a debate, so I don't need to debate philosophers again. they are too clever
Quoting @mohitban47
🚨 Excited to announce the 'UNC Symposium on AI and Society'! 🙂
