AI has development backwards, according to me, and I stand by it. A recent piece by @SilverJacket discusses why world models are necessary, especially for building machines that learn and think like humans.

@SilverJacket questions whether large language models can reach artificial general intelligence or if we need world models. The latest news feature for @ScienceMagazine covers this topic. Thanks to Jared Kaplan, @ylecun, @PimDeWitte, @AdamJelley2, @janexwang, @shlomifruchter, @LakeBrenden, @yukez, @merettm, @AnthropicAI, @amilabs, @gen_intuition, @GoogleDeepMind, @OpenAI, and others.

